        {
          "id": "bible:theographic:meshullam_2037",
          "nativeName": "Meshullam",
          "name": "Meshullam",
          "aliases": [],
          "unit": "Curated Biblical named-entity/person record",
          "sourceRecordKey": "meshullam_2037",
          "sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased": 2024,
          "sourceRefs": [
            "theographic:CSV/People.csv"
          ],
          "verseRefs": [
            "Neh.12.13"
          ],
          "genderAsCurated": "Male",
          "ambiguousAsCurated": true,
          "disambiguationNote": "is a Biblical masculine name meaning \"Befriended\". In the Old Testament the name Meshullam was borne by eleven characters: Meshullam (One of the chief Gadites in Bashan in the time of Jotham (1 Chronicles 5:13). Grandfather of Shaphan, \"the scribe\", in the reign of Josiah (2 Kings 22:3). A priest, father of Hilkiah (1 Chronicles 9:11),(Nehemiah 11:11), in the reign of Ammon; called Shallum in (1 Chronicles 6:12). A Levite of the family of Kohath (2 Chronicles 34:12), in the reign of Josiah. A son of Elpaal. (1 Chronicles 8:17). One of two sons of Zerubbabel, the other being Hananiah. (1 Chronicles 3:19) A priest, head of the House of Ezra. (Nehemiah 12:13). A chief priest (Nehemiah 12:16). One of the leading Levites in the time of Ezra (Ezra 8:16). A priest (1 Chronicles 9:12). One of the principal Israelites who supported Ezra when expounding the law to the people (Nehemiah 8:4).)",
          "generation": null,
          "absoluteChronology": null,
          "musicalAssignment": null,
          "historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed": false,
          "curatedChronologyNotAdopted": {
            "birthYear": "",
            "deathYear": "",
            "basis": "Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."
          },
          "tradition": "Biblical curated/verse-local comparison",
          "witnessId": "Theographic-KJV-comparison",
          "position": {
            "generation": null,
            "sequence": 2024,
            "cyclicCoordinate": null,
            "orientation": null
          },
          "assertionLayer": "curator-or-textual-occurrence",
          "exceptions": [
            "is a Biblical masculine name meaning \"Befriended\". In the Old Testament the name Meshullam was borne by eleven characters: Meshullam (One of the chief Gadites in Bashan in the time of Jotham (1 Chronicles 5:13). Grandfather of Shaphan, \"the scribe\", in the reign of Josiah (2 Kings 22:3). A priest, father of Hilkiah (1 Chronicles 9:11),(Nehemiah 11:11), in the reign of Ammon; called Shallum in (1 Chronicles 6:12). A Levite of the family of Kohath (2 Chronicles 34:12), in the reign of Josiah. A son of Elpaal. (1 Chronicles 8:17). One of two sons of Zerubbabel, the other being Hananiah. (1 Chronicles 3:19) A priest, head of the House of Ezra. (Nehemiah 12:13). A chief priest (Nehemiah 12:16). One of the leading Levites in the time of Ezra (Ezra 8:16). A priest (1 Chronicles 9:12). One of the principal Israelites who supported Ezra when expounding the law to the people (Nehemiah 8:4).)"
          ],
          "globalSunnyAddress": null,
          "sourceOccurrenceRetained": true
